Adjustments:

DONE - Dungeon movement/render crashes and lockups fixed.
       The ANSI door renderer could write outside the 3D wall buffer while
       drawing certain door views, causing carrier drops, crashes, or
       movement/redraw lockups during dungeon navigation. Door detail writes
       are now kept inside the guarded render path and bounds checked before
       writing to wall[][].
DONE - Combat awarded 0 EXP because monster EXP values were blank.
       Implemented initial monster EXP rewards using Gold / 256 baseline.
DONE - Cleric paid healing no longer allows overhealing past actual max HP.
       The old 250 HP service cap remains, but healing now also respects
       the player's missing HP and only charges for HP actually restored.

        HP 32/37, enter 999  -> heals 5, charges 10 pp, ends 37/37
        HP 10/37, enter 999  -> heals 27, charges 54 pp, ends 37/37
        HP 100/400, enter 999 -> heals 250, charges 500 pp, ends 350/400

VERIFIED: Old DONE list mostly still true.
            - "give items/gold" appears to be gold/PP only; no item-give function found.
            - "Write on wall" is currently B/ScriBble, not W.
VERIFIED - Store red-list equip restriction appears working.
           Inventory colours indicate item type, not class usability.
           Example: Cloak of Dathedi is green in shop because usable,
                    red in inventory because it is ARMOUR.
VERIFIED - Drinking water does not make the player drunk.
           Repeated water purchases left the player sober/healthy.
           Alcohol correctly sets drunk status, with no observed HP drain
           or combat side effects during current testing.
           My testing:
           Water x10+:
            - remained sober
            - State stayed Healthy
            - HP did not move

            Ice Ale:
            - correctly changed status to drunk
            - drunk status persisted through movement/screens/combat
            - HP did not drop
            - no combat-side drunk/poison weirdness observed 
VERIFIED - Object healing does not appear to exceed player max HP.
           Item/special healing checks current HP before use and the shared
           player heal path caps HP at maxhp.
           Separate Cleric paid-healing over-cap was fixed independently.
VERIFIED - Leave/re-enter AC initialization could not be reproduced.
           Current code loads player equipment, recalculates AC with acplyr()
           before restoring dungeon play, and the status panel displays the
           recalculated live AC value.
VERIFIED - Checked for Dragon Amulet references: no hard-coded source reference found. 
           No Dragon Amulet exists in the current FSE object database. 
           Original note may refer to older/missing object DAT test data.

REQUIRES VALIDATION - Adjusted Wizard/Cleric guild spell-learn slot pre-check.
                      The learn menu was checking (9 - selection) * 5,
                      which can read past level-1 spell slots. Changed to
                      match casting menu slot mapping: (8 - selection) * 5.
REQUIRES VALIDATION - Adjusted Cleric paid-healing cap.
                      Paid healing accepted the requested heal amount,
                      charged for that amount, then only capped final HP
                      at the old 250 service limit. Healing now also
                      respects the player's actual missing HP and only
                      charges for HP actually restored.
REQUIRES VALIDATION - Adjusted Cleric remove-curse slot tracking.
                      Remove curse was finding equipped cursed items, but
                      stored matching inventory slots using the inventory
                      index instead of the packed menu/list index. Changed
                      the list to pack matching slots so cost calculation
                      and uncurse processing target the intended items.
REQUIRES VALIDATION - Duplicate players after combat were not reproduced in current testing.
                      Added a conservative combat cleanup safety check so players
                      leaving encounters have their in-combat flag cleared.
                      Monitor during v0.63 alpha testing for any remaining duplicate
                      player display or stale combat-entry behaviour.


v0.63 alpha candidate work-in-progress

Goal:
Stabilize Worlds of Darkness enough for wider alpha testing.

Fixed for next alpha candidate:

- Fixed ANSI door renderer bounds issue that could crash movement/redraw.
- Fixed FSD editor list alignment and cursor placement.
- Fixed FSD Race editor Cast % display.
- Fixed FSD Spell editor name bleed from fixed-width spellname fields.
- Restored monster EXP rewards using an initial gold/256 baseline.
- Confirmed combat EXP now awards during combat and appears on player status.
- Confirmed basic dungeon movement, combat, EXP awards, and status progression are stable in current testing.
- Verified class-restricted store items cannot be used/readied when not valid for the player class.
- Fixed Wizard/Cleric guild spell-learn slot pre-check to match casting slot layout.
- Fixed drunkenness being processed as poison after drinking alcohol.
- Fixed Cleric paid healing so it respects the player’s actual max HP and only charges for HP actually restored.
- Fixed Cleric remove-curse slot tracking so equipped cursed items are correctly costed and uncursed.
- Fixed wearable rings and amulets not appearing in the dungeon Ready and combat Equip item-selection menus.
- Added combat cleanup safety so players leaving encounters have their in-combat flag cleared, reducing the chance of stale/duplicate player entries after combat.

Still under review:

- Validate Wizard/Cleric guild spell learning in-game once guild access is reached.
- Validate Cleric paid healing cap in-game once Cleric/Church access is reached.
- Validate Cleric/Church poison curing in-game once Cleric/Church access is reached.
- Validate Cleric/Church remove-curse flow in-game once Cleric/Church access is reached.
- Validate wearable rings and amulets can be readied/equipped in-game once suitable test items are available.
- Monitor duplicate-player reports after combat during v0.63 alpha testing; not reproduced in current testing, but a conservative combat cleanup safety check was added.
